 "source": "https://github.com/sysjust-xq/vscode-xs (MIT) commit c6101a57676990160de656171bd72638d5758102, 2023-04-26, file xs/syntaxes/xs.tmLanguage.json; cross-checked 2026-08-25 against https://xshelp.xq.com.tw/XSHelp/ category lists (server-rendered anchors only; JS-populated lists such as TECHINDEXFUNC contribute little) and per-function pages fetched for SetPosition/Position/Filled/FilledAvgPrice/AddSpread/Market/Buy/Sell/Average/XAverage/RSI/ATR/Highest/Lowest/BarsLast/CrossOver/BarFreq/IsSessionFirstBar/IsSessionLastBar/EnterMarketCloseTime/Once/IntrabarPersist/Input/Var/Cross/If-Then-Else/Time/Date.",
 "notes": "XS is case-insensitive (grammar uses (?i)); match tokens case-insensitively. Comments: line '//' to end of line; block '{ ... }' (nesting attempted by grammar, do not rely on it). Strings: double quotes only, no escape sequences in the grammar ((\")[^\"]*(\")); single quotes are NOT a string delimiter in the grammar even though the editor auto-closes them - flag any '. Statement terminator ';'. Assignment and equality are both '='; '<>' is not-equal; '==' and '!=' do not exist; ':=' appears only in the named parameter form label:=\"...\". Bar-back indexing is name[n] with n>=0 integer or expression. Multi-word operators: 'cross over' / 'cross above' / 'cross under' / 'cross below' (also 'crosses'); each word is a separate token in keywords. 'Value0..Value999' and 'Condition0..Condition999' are built-in series variables (patterns Value[0-9]{1,3} / Condition[0-9]{1,3}); 'Plot1..Plot99', 'OutputField', 'SetOutputName' carry an optional numeric suffix. Names in 'functions' that come only from xshelp (not the grammar) are listed in the source string above. Any identifier not in these lists must be declared with input:/var:/variable:/array: in the file before use; user identifiers are [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*. Full-width punctuation (，；（）：「」) is a hard error. EasyLanguage-only names that do NOT exist in XS and must be flagged: MarketPosition, EntryPrice, AvgEntryPrice, BarsSinceEntry, SetStopLoss, SetProfitTarget, SetExitOnClose, SetDollarTrailing, SetPercentTrailing, CurrentContracts, MaxPositionProfit, OpenPositionProfit, NetProfit, next bar, this bar, contracts, shares, stop, limit, SessionEndTime, Buy to cover, Sell short, EntryDate, EntryTime, ExitPrice. Note the words Buy/Sell/Short/Cover DO exist in XS but as position-delta functions Buy(qty[,price]) etc., never as EL 'Buy next bar at market' statements. Operators: the grammar's operator regex lists only * - + = <= >= <> += -= ; the linter must ALSO accept / < > ( ) [ ] , : and unary minus (division and < > appear in official examples, e.g. Floor(amount*10/Close), Close > Open). Declared-variable series semantics (x[1], 'x cross over y' on a var) are assumed from EasyLanguage lineage and the IntrabarPersist doc, not explicitly documented - templates flag them UNVERIFIED.",
